# Teachers who become what they are said not to be
#
# Russell and Wittgenstein teach philosophy. One rule says a teacher is not a
# unicorn when the current graph does not say they are, and another rule turns
# that statement into the very claim it denies. Russell's derived claim
# contradicts the absence used to derive it, so eyeron trips an inference fuse
# and returns no conclusions. The example shows a negative dependency cycle
# through scoped negation, decided for each individual.

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix : <https://example.org/course#> .

# Facts
:philosophy :teacher :russell .
:philosophy :teacher :wittgenstein .

# A teacher is not a unicorn when the current graph does not say so.
{
    ?course :teacher ?x .
    ?scope log:notIncludes {
        ?x :isA :Unicorn .
    } .
} => {
    ?x :isNot :Unicorn .
} .

# Whatever is not a unicorn is a unicorn.
{
    ?x :isNot :Unicorn .
} => {
    ?x :isA :Unicorn .
} .
